Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Bundles", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"70b5b5ff-6322-45dc-9c07-c34d38d8fe09"],

Cell["\<\
We start with a finite graph and a projection of its vertices. Equal fibers, \
lift existence, unique lifting and bundle structure are separate properties. \
Sections and complete connections add choices to this data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d8a7a99b-612f-46a6-8917-b1c000c84ba3"],

Cell["Topological language and finite readings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ac197d3a-1abd-4d39-a217-74c0e4950094"],

Cell["\<\
The finite object is a graph with a vertex projection. The following \
dictionary distinguishes its exact conditions from the additional structures \
of continuous topology.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"494cd512-2b8f-4603-ac9e-3f3568c6623b"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "72bc41f0-3e08-4026-9a29-fc33dd7defd9"], Cell[
    "Topological notion", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"b0f3682a-0bf2-4753-9a66-e565b01dc4e2"],
     Cell["Finite infra reading", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"4b134aa9-342b-4acf-a22b-965f15603a6f"],
     Cell["Qualification", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"343b9ac2-6d1b-4a50-9ecb-2f21c9266810"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "bdaf824b-38eb-435d-ae0e-16b133a7edbc"], Cell[
    "Projection from total space to base", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "a7ff87ae-2605-4903-8749-700f0e930f30"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberedGraph with InfraTotalSpace, InfraBaseSpace and InfraProjection\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5bfec424-bb48-4177-848c-0267a14980cd"], 
    Cell["\<\
The base graph is reconstructed from projected edges; no topology is part of \
the inert object.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6159d150-bd48-4908-9dea-face027ecfcf"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "421f8e03-ec43-4697-9db7-3ea3ab9f33b3"], Cell[
    "Serre or Hurewicz fibration", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "c7068b30-4edf-4a10-b516-a124bbcfbfa6"], Cell["\<\
InfraFibrationQ asks for a lift of every base edge from every starting vertex\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a9eb8f66-e4c8-4337-b1b9-12cd2a349958"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is weak edge-lift existence, not a homotopy-lifting axiom.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8069e482-b7ea-4e6b-af41-5db7b03415c1"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "31ddcf5f-05f0-474b-b007-e786543fe8d8"], Cell[
    "Covering space", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "a9351d4c-6d8c-44dc-956e-d1ce09cbba29"], Cell["\<\
InfraCoveringQ gives edgeless fibers and a bijection on vertex neighbourhoods\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a02e5d6f-e09b-4988-9727-185e56e5a429"], 
    Cell["\<\
The graph-covering condition has the usual covering interpretation under \
graph realization. Sheet counts can differ across base components.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"92c389fd-a828-4265-b95d-7547798c44c8"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "54d68af1-e183-45f1-b357-3642da5f8765"], Cell[
    "Fiber bundle", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0f4d2f56-fd8b-45f8-b8a1-604167f71211"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberBundleQ gives a common fiber graph and adjacency-preserving \
transverse matchings\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"11bd91b0-d8ab-461b-8c04-0ea8740dd6f7"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is an edgewise Cartesian graph bundle. Realizing its edges alone does \
not supply topological product charts or filled squares.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"636116ff-956e-4d58-bf82-b369607b1734"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7b7c501e-45f0-468d-8449-0651ccbceb91"], Cell[
    "Section", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "095b3570-fe9d-48c9-be75-02bda8d4a787"], Cell[
    "InfraSection chooses a right inverse on a base domain", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"da857f6d-94ea-4a72-9f6d-0992e711bcec"], Cell["\<\
InfraContinuousSectionQ asks for adjacency preservation on that domain.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"9017b3a5-fdfd-4495-aeb0-2a28825172c5"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2dcdb4c6-de48-48a1-9b47-33a357411c21"], Cell[
    "Connection and parallel transport", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "08f6b3a9-c892-4817-891e-f32da9fba487"], Cell["\<\
InfraConnection selects complete fiber matchings; transport composes them\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"84f18a4f-7223-434f-83aa-3214e517ca64"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is finite bijective transport. Preserving a fiber graph is an additional \
condition.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"9a202f1a-8775-44b8-b2b0-8909dc91c407"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "1b5d94c0-4a0a-496a-a7ab-ee0d430e35f8"], Cell[
    "Infra-only transverse local conditions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e1c5f2b-e051-47e5-afe3-2294cc09891f"], Cell["\<\
InfraAtMostOneEdgeLiftQ and InfraFibrationQ read injectivity and surjectivity \
on transverse neighbours\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"73bd6f08-b7b6-4cc7-8c08-b9fbceac99c9"], 
    Cell["\<\
Vertical neighbours are excluded; the conditions do not assert local \
injectivity or surjectivity in a chosen topology.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ec66d5e6-5590-4e4b-8633-c4fccbea5279"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "b837be8a-24aa-46bc-9e58-2a0fcc132479"], Cell[
    "Infra-only multiplicity and equitable partition", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"43d7ef58-2f86-4340-afb6-627085dde111"], Cell["\<\
InfraEdgeLiftMultiplicity counts transverse neighbours, including zeros\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"f7866fde-ba92-4fc7-afdb-3799c292a61c"], 
    Cell["\<\
Constancy within each fiber is transverse equitability; full equitability \
also needs constant vertical degree.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b6f5a498-a07d-4cfa-bd0e-bd0b04b118e5"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"62888823-d4ee-4c30-a0ac-\
0a19c8f6d4ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the continuous definitions, see ",
 ButtonBox["Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Sections 1.3 and 4.2",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"], None}],
 ". The finite definitions and their implications are developed below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"626cd701-3b18-45b8-8a77-8502875b9ad2"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"341d0050-c09c-4e2b-ac05-c94c77e5d499"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", " ", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", " ", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d216cd40-0d8f-4207-9f3e-65b067cb9eeb"],

Cell["Total space, projection and fibers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"63446584-dba3-4743-a2a2-df9bdaaad4a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["fibered graph", "TI"],
 " consists of a finite simple undirected unweighted untagged graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd56f6d6-3353-4820-a517-df62e7d4ca26"],
 " and a map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8bc2bc0-08e8-4990-a302-f61bd2cf90c8"],
 " on its vertices. The ",
 StyleBox["base graph", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9f60be0-d337-42d9-88c3-753d4b7f94c0"],
 " has vertex set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b2148811-78fc-4d6f-acc4-aa5789538fe8"],
 ". Distinct base vertices are adjacent exactly when some total edge joins \
their preimages. The ",
 StyleBox["fiber", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03e0ec4f-e9d8-4ebe-950d-261f11fc919c"],
 " is the induced graph on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a59b1a1-a7cc-4f10-9120-024f4a3a5c58"],
 ". A total edge is ",
 StyleBox["vertical", "TI"],
 " when both endpoints project to the same vertex, and ",
 StyleBox["transverse", "TI"],
 " otherwise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5510dec-e475-4333-8bce-ddaa2fcfdf1f"],

Cell["\<\
The object carries no drawing, connection or lifting axiom. The base includes \
isolated projection values, and projection collapses vertical edges. The \
empty graph with empty projection is allowed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a25eb13e-ee31-4f2c-bf66-e06f169b6b8a"],

