Cell["Sections and extensions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3fca6561-b65d-42ec-9fb3-a39562c548a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["section on a domain", "TI"],
 " chooses one total vertex over each base vertex in that domain. It is ",
 StyleBox["continuous", "TI"],
 " when every base edge within the domain maps to a total edge. A partial \
section fixes values to be preserved by an extension."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ee45d17-e265-48fe-a95e-8437b069da31"],

Cell["\<\
The default section class is set-theoretic on every overload. A domain list \
restricts the target; an inert section supplies prescribed values and \
requests extension over the whole base. The continuous property is requested \
explicitly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5d14bd8-085e-421e-8f40-77bf03de99c6"],

Cell["\<\
Complete joins let a partial section extend continuously in every choice of \
the remaining fibers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"007825be-c449-49ee-9517-bd053bb4a723"],

