Cell[TextData[{
 "The retained flat-connection predicate tests ",
 StyleBox["trivial global monodromy", "TI"],
 ": every closed base walk acts identically. This is equivalent to every \
horizontal leaf projecting injectively. Indeed, two vertices in one leaf over \
the same base vertex give a lifted closed walk between them. Conversely, a \
closed walk with distinct lift endpoints places two such vertices in one leaf."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e5f898c8-858e-4e72-a09f-14c439c10c0b"],

Cell["\<\
Curvature needs a specified family of faces and their boundary loops. A graph \
alone supplies no such family. The global monodromy predicate therefore does \
not replace a face-based curvature definition.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c2acbf7-138c-4928-8824-5bf8ab4fde31"],

Cell["Three views of one object", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c3ea0204-8346-40d7-871e-6b603be39a33"],

Cell["\<\
Circular fibers, upright three-dimensional fibers and the total graph's own \
layout display the same finite object. Highlights preserve their meaning in \
every view.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6127f063-001a-426f-8240-fdb7beb80cf2"],

